{
	"info": {
		"_postman_id": "encryption-api-collection",
		"name": "Encryption API - Production",
		"description": "Complete Postman collection for testing the Encryption API with AWS Cognito authentication.\n\n## Setup Instructions\n\n1. Import this collection into Postman\n2. Create a new environment or use the provided environment variables\n3. Set your username and password in the environment\n4. Run the \"Login\" request first to get JWT tokens\n5. Tokens are automatically saved to environment variables\n6. All other requests will use the saved tokens automatically\n\n## Environment Variables\n\nRequired:\n- `base_url`: https://3tyukwdl69.execute-api.us-east-1.amazonaws.com\n- `username`: Your email address\n- `password`: Your password\n\nAuto-populated (after login):\n- `id_token`: JWT ID token (used for API authentication)\n- `access_token`: JWT access token\n- `refresh_token`: JWT refresh token (valid for 30 days)\n- `encrypted_id`: Last encrypted data ID (for decrypt testing)",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
	"item": [
		{
			"name": "Authentication",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Login",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"exec": [
									"// Parse response",
									"const jsonData = pm.response.json();",
									"",
									"// Save tokens to environment variables",
									"if (jsonData.idToken) {",
									"    pm.environment.set('id_token', jsonData.idToken);",
									"    console.log('✓ ID Token saved to environment');",
									"}",
									"",
									"if (jsonData.accessToken) {",
									"    pm.environment.set('access_token', jsonData.accessToken);",
									"    console.log('✓ Access Token saved to environment');",
									"}",
									"",
									"if (jsonData.refreshToken) {",
									"    pm.environment.set('refresh_token', jsonData.refreshToken);",
									"    console.log('✓ Refresh Token saved to environment');",
									"}",
									"",
									"// Verify response",
									"pm.test('Status code is 200', function () {",
									"    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
									"});",
									"",
									"pm.test('Response contains idToken', function () {",
									"    pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('idToken');",
									"});",
									"",
									"pm.test('Response contains accessToken', function () {",
									"    pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('accessToken');",
									"});",
									"",
									"pm.test('Response contains refreshToken', function () {",
									"    pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('refreshToken');",
									"});",
									"",
									"pm.test('Token expires in 3600 seconds (1 hour)', function () {",
									"    pm.expect(jsonData.expiresIn).to.eql(3600);",
									"});"
								],
								"type": "text/javascript"
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Content-Type",
								"value": "application/json"
							}
						],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"{{username}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{password}}\"\n}"
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{base_url}}/api/auth/login",
							"host": [
								"{{base_url}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"api",
								"auth",
								"login"
							]
						},
						"description": "Authenticate with AWS Cognito and receive JWT tokens.\n\n**Required Environment Variables:**\n- `username`: Your email address\n- `password`: Your password\n\n**Returns:**\n- `idToken`: Use this in Authorization header for API calls\n- `accessToken`: Additional access token\n- `refreshToken`: Use to refresh tokens without re-entering password\n- `expiresIn`: Token expiration time (3600 seconds = 1 hour)\n\n**Auto-saved to Environment:**\nAll tokens are automatically saved to environment variables for use in subsequent requests."
					},
					"response": []
				},
				{
					"name": "Refresh Token",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"exec": [
									"// Parse response",
									"const jsonData = pm.response.json();",
									"",
									"// Update tokens in environment",
									"if (jsonData.idToken) {",
									"    pm.environment.set('id_token', jsonData.idToken);",
									"    console.log('✓ ID Token refreshed');",
									"}",
									"",
									"if (jsonData.accessToken) {",
									"    pm.environment.set('access_token', jsonData.accessToken);",
									"    console.log('✓ Access Token refreshed');",
									"}",
									"",
									"// Verify response",
									"pm.test('Status code is 200', function () {",
									"    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
									"});",
									"",
									"pm.test('Response contains new idToken', function () {",
									"    pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('idToken');",
									"});",
									"",
									"pm.test('Response contains new accessToken', function () {",
									"    pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('accessToken');",
									"});"
								],
								"type": "text/javascript"
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Content-Type",
								"value": "application/json"
							}
						],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n  \"refreshToken\": \"{{refresh_token}}\"\n}"
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{base_url}}/api/auth/refresh",
							"host": [
								"{{base_url}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"api",
								"auth",
								"refresh"
							]
						},
						"description": "Refresh your access token without re-entering credentials.\n\n**Required Environment Variable:**\n- `refresh_token`: The refresh token from login (valid for 30 days)\n\n**Returns:**\n- New `idToken` and `accessToken`\n- Tokens are automatically updated in environment variables"
					},
					"response": []
				}
			],
			"description": "Authentication endpoints for obtaining and refreshing JWT tokens via AWS Cognito."
		},
		{
