		{
			"name": "Encryption",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Encrypt Data",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"exec": [
									"const jsonData = pm.response.json();",
									"",
									"// Save encrypted ID for decrypt testing",
									"if (jsonData.id) {",
									"    pm.environment.set('encrypted_id', jsonData.id);",
									"    console.log('✓ Encrypted ID saved: ' + jsonData.id);",
									"}",
									"",
									"pm.test('Status code is 201', function () {",
									"    pm.response.to.have.status(201);",
									"});",
									"",
									"pm.test('Response contains ID', function () {",
									"    pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('id');",
									"});",
									"",
									"pm.test('Response contains success message', function () {",
									"    pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('message');",
									"    pm.expect(jsonData.message).to.include('encrypted');",
									"});",
									"",
									"pm.test('Response contains userId', function () {",
									"    pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('userId');",
									"});",
									"",
									"pm.test('Response contains timestamp', function () {",
									"    pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('timestamp');",
									"});"
								],
								"type": "text/javascript"
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"auth": {
							"type": "bearer",
							"bearer": [
								{
									"key": "token",
									"value": "{{id_token}}",
									"type": "string"
								}
							]
						},
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Content-Type",
								"value": "application/json"
							}
						],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n  \"plainText\": \"My sensitive credit card number is 1234-5678-9012-3456\"\n}"
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{base_url}}/api/encrypt",
							"host": [
								"{{base_url}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"api",
								"encrypt"
							]
						},
						"description": "Encrypt sensitive data and store it securely.\n\n**Authentication:** Required (JWT Bearer token)\n\n**Request Body:**\n```json\n{\n  \"plainText\": \"Your sensitive data\"\n}\n```\n\n**Returns:**\n- `id`: Encrypted data ID (use this to decrypt later)\n- `message`: Success confirmation\n- `userId`: Your user ID (from Cognito JWT)\n- `timestamp`: When the data was encrypted\n\n**Security:**\n- Data is encrypted with AES-256-GCM\n- Each user can only access their own encrypted data\n- Encryption keys are stored in AWS Secrets Manager"
					},
					"response": []
				},
				{
					"name": "Decrypt Data",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"exec": [
									"const jsonData = pm.response.json();",
									"",
									"pm.test('Status code is 200', function () {",
									"    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
									"});",
									"",
									"pm.test('Response contains ID', function () {",
									"    pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('id');",
									"});",
									"",
									"pm.test('Response contains plainText', function () {",
									"    pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('plainText');",
									"});",
									"",
									"pm.test('Response contains userId', function () {",
									"    pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('userId');",
									"});",
									"",
									"pm.test('Response contains timestamp', function () {",
									"    pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('timestamp');",
									"});",
									"",
									"// Verify decrypted data matches what we encrypted",
									"if (pm.environment.get('last_encrypted_text')) {",
									"    pm.test('Decrypted text matches original', function () {",
									"        pm.expect(jsonData.plainText).to.eql(pm.environment.get('last_encrypted_text'));",
									"    });",
									"}"
								],
								"type": "text/javascript"
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"auth": {
							"type": "bearer",
							"bearer": [
								{
									"key": "token",
									"value": "{{id_token}}",
									"type": "string"
								}
							]
						},
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{base_url}}/api/decrypt/:id",
							"host": [
								"{{base_url}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"api",
								"decrypt",
								":id"
							],
							"variable": [
								{
									"key": "id",
									"value": "{{encrypted_id}}",
									"description": "The ID returned from the encrypt endpoint"
								}
							]
						},
						"description": "Retrieve and decrypt previously encrypted data.\n\n**Authentication:** Required (JWT Bearer token)\n\n**Path Parameter:**\n- `id`: The encrypted data ID from the encrypt endpoint\n\n**Returns:**\n- `id`: The encrypted data ID\n- `plainText`: Your original unencrypted data\n- `userId`: Your user ID\n- `timestamp`: When the data was retrieved\n\n**Security:**\n- You can only decrypt your own data\n- Attempting to decrypt another user's data returns 403 Forbidden\n- Non-existent IDs return 404 Not Found"
					},
					"response": []
				},
